    "page": "fetched once by every validator itself, and the body of that one answer is what is judged: a failed fetch or a status outside 200 to 299 stores nothing and takes no credit; then the first 128000 bytes of the body read as UTF-8, every tag removed and the text after a script or style tag dropped, the whitespace of the first 32000 characters collapsed to single spaces, and the first 4000 characters of that judged; fp is the first 16 hex characters of their sha256, and an accepted page's first 1200 characters are how it is shown to every later reader",
